Fixed the login callback stopping at "Signing you in…" forever. The route renders `Callback` as a bare component, so nothing passed it the optional `onToken` prop it needed to do anything with the token it had just fetched — the exchange succeeded, the backend answered 200, and the page sat there. The component had no test at all, which is how it shipped that way.

Signing in is now the default rather than something a caller has to supply. The token is dispatched as Volto's own `LOGIN_SUCCESS`, which is the whole sign-in: `persistAuthToken` subscribes to the store at client start and writes any new `userSession.token` out to the cookie, so writing that cookie here would be a second implementation of it. The browser is then sent to wherever the flow started, by a full load rather than a router push, because everything rendered up to that point was rendered for an anonymous user. A caller passing `onToken` still overrides all of it. @ericof
